      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)=5\\sqrt{x},$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 1,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin.",
      "worked_solution": "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=5\\sqrt{x},\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot 5\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}5{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {1}^{5/2}-0 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$",
